**There is no threshold.** Workers scale from 0 to infinity with no configuration changes. The architecture is designed so doubling traffic requires zero code changes and near-zero cost increase.

## VPC & Queue Integration

### OverSeer Manifold (VPC Service)

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Service Name | `overseer-manifold` |
| Service ID | `019ce99b-5f34-7902-9513-9b26bc4755c8` |
| Host | `localhost` |
| HTTP Port | `11434` |
| Tunnel | Little Nate Twin Engine (`d40e5315-4d8a-44b8-a432-debc36750636`) |

Workers that need Home GPU inference can call the VPC service directly — no public URL, no VPS hop. The VPC routes through the Cloudflare backbone to the tunnel, which terminates at `localhost:11434` (Ollama) on the Mac.

**Workers that should bind to `overseer-manifold`:**

| Worker | Use Case |
|---|---|
| `nate-summon-worker` | TENSION/DEEP_TENSION queries → 70B depth |
| `nate-voice-edge` | TTS voice clone (future, when XTTS VPC service added) |
| `nate-cron-worker` | Crystal pre-warm, hallucination review batches |

### ln-echo-relay (Queue)

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Queue Name | `ln-echo-relay` |
| Queue ID | `218cde12f4f04af58a0bab077fe9fbb0` |
| Purpose | Async task dispatch between Workers, VPS, and Mac |

The queue decouples timing between the cloud brains. Producers (any Worker or VPS agent) enqueue tasks. Consumers (Mac-bound Workers, VPS agents) drain them at their own pace.

**When to use the queue vs. direct VPC call:**

| Scenario | Use |
|---|---|
| User-facing, latency-sensitive (<2s budget) | Direct VPC call to `overseer-manifold` |
| Background processing, can tolerate 30s+ | Queue via `ln-echo-relay` |
| Mac is offline, task can wait 24h | Queue (messages persist with TTL) |
| Fire-and-forget (analytics, archival) | Queue |

### Rules

11. **Workers calling `overseer-manifold` must have a timeout.** If the Mac is asleep or tunnel is disconnected, the VPC call hangs. Workers should time out at 30s and fall back to the next inference provider.

12. **Queue consumers must be idempotent.** Messages may be delivered more than once. Use `task_id` (UUID) for deduplication.

13. **Queue message TTL is 24 hours.** Messages older than 24h are dead-lettered. If the Mac was offline for >24h, some synthesis/batch work may be lost — the VPS's next crystallizer/archive cycle will re-enqueue anything still needed.

## Cloudflare Realtime — TURN + Serverless SFU + MoQ Relay

Three Cloudflare Realtime services provide the media plane for all real-time audio/video features. See `cloudflare-realtime-webrtc.mdc` for full credentials and architecture.

| Service | ID | Workers That Use It |
|---|---|---|
| TURN (`restless-math-4d7b`) | Token ID `17704023fbb65016f12abb900048b359` | `nate-voice-edge` (credential generation) |
| SFU (`aged-block-6976`) | App ID `8d23ce5179380706d203fd16e1b88a1a` | `nate-voice-edge` (session proxy), `nate-summon-worker` (summon calls) |
| MoQ Relay | `draft-14.cloudflare.mediaoverquic.com` | `nate-voice-edge` (Nate voice publish), `nate-summon-worker` (coherence stream) |

**`nate-voice-edge` gains three new responsibilities:**
- `POST /api/voice/turn-credentials` — proxies TURN credential generation (returns `iceServers` to clients)
- `POST /api/voice/sfu/*` — proxies SFU session/track API calls (clients never see the SFU token)
- `POST /api/voice/moq/publish` — publishes Nate's generated voice to MoQ namespace for subscriber fan-out

**MoQ role separation from SFU:**
- **SFU** handles peer-to-peer media (family members hear each other)
- **MoQ** handles Nate-to-many voice delivery (one publish, infinite subscribers at 302 PoPs)
- The VPS/Mac generates the voice, publishes ONCE to MoQ, and never manages distribution

### Rules

14. **SFU API token must never reach the client.** All SFU calls are proxied through Workers or the VPS backend.
15. **TURN credentials are ephemeral.** Generate per-session via the credential API, never hardcode.
16. **SFU replaces Zoom for DOJO/classroom video.** No Zoom dependency required for multi-party sessions.
17. **MoQ is Nate-to-many only.** Never route member-to-member audio through MoQ — that's SFU's job. MoQ carries Nate's generated voice, coherence signals, and escalation alerts.
18. **MoQ namespaces must be session-scoped.** Always `sanctuary/{sessionId}/nate-voice-{userId}`, never bare `sanctuary/nate-voice`. Prevents cross-session bleed.
19. **Global MoQ tracks are anonymized.** `global/coherence-aggregate` and `global/cycle-signals` contain only aggregate metrics, never user identifiers.
